  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-07-12T06:13:00.973Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Attempting to access the material used for the sky crashes scripts silently without throwing any errors. I've tried three different methods of accessing the material, all of which result in a crash: 1. directly feeding the material into the script as a parameter, 2. Getting the sharedMaterial of an object using the same material as the skybox, and 3. Using RenderSettings.skybox. I'm guessing this is probably due to default scene objects being protected, but we should really have access to modifying the sky's material. I'm using SDK3 version 2020.06.16.20.53 and the latest version of U#.",
